  "body": " Nonlinear Models  Volume  You are designing a new coffee maker. The coffee filter must be 8.4 centimeters tall and shaped like a cone. The volume of the filter will therefore depend on how wide the opening is (the radius of the cone).   Write a formula for the filter's volume in terms of its widest radius (at the top of the filter). (Hint: Look up the formula for the volume of a cone.)  Simplify your formula by multiplying the constants together.  Complete the table of values. Round the volumes to one decimal place.    (cm)  1  2  3  4  5  6  7  8  (cm )           Look at the table of values. If you double the radius of the filter, by what factor does the volume increase?  Write and solve an equation to answer the question: If the volume of the filter is 302.4 cubic centimeters, what is its radius?  Use technology to graph the volume equation. (Use the table of values to help you choose a window.) Sketch your graph on paper, including scales on the axes). Label the coordinates of the point on the graph that corresponds to the filter in part (d).    Extraction of Roots   Solve each equation by extraction of roots.       Solve. Give your answers two ways: (i) exact values and (ii) approximations rounded to thousandths.      Solve each formula for the requested variable.  2(3) Ask students how we should handle the fractions in these two formulas.   for  for     Compound Interest  Cyril would like to invest $100 for two years in a money market account that pays interest compounded annually.    Write a formula for the balance, , of Cyril's account after two years in terms of the interest rate, .  Complete the table showing Cyril's account balance after two years for various interest rates.                 If Cyril would like to have $125 in two years, what interest rate must the account pay?     Checkpoint   Sketch a graph that illustrates why a quadratic equation can have two solutions.  In part (d) of Activity 1, what technique did you use to solve the equation?  Explain how to deal with the fractions in part (3) of Activity 2.  Explain how you found the solution to part (c) of Activity 3, being careful to list all the steps you used.   "
