  "body": " The Absolute Value Function  Solving Absolute Value Equations  We'll solve the equation in three different ways: with a graph, wth a number line, and with algebra.   Solution by graphing   Graph with technology, and copy the graph onto the grid below.  grid [-10,10]x[-4,10]  Sketch the horizontal line on your graph.  Find the points on the graph of that have . (How many points are there?) What are the -coordinates of those two points? These are the solutions.   Next we'll use a number line to solve the equation.   Translate the equation into a sentence about distance.  Locate 3 on the number line below, and find two points at a distance of 5 units from 3.  number line -10 to 10  What are the -coordinates of those two points?    Finally, we'll use algebra to sove the equation. Recall the definition of absolute value:   Now substitute for :  Thus, the equation has two parts:   Solve each equation to get two solutions.   Solve the equation in three different ways:   By graphing .  grid [-10,10]x[-4,10]  By using a number line.  number line -10 to 10  By using algebra.     Solving Absolute Value Inequalities  We'll solve the inequality in three different ways: with a graph, wth a number line, and with algebra.   Solution by graphing   Refer to your graph of in Activity 2, and shade the points on the graph that have .  grid [-10,10]x[-4,10]  Now shade the portion of the -axis that corresponds to those points. (Are the endpoints included in the solution set?) Write your answer with interval notation.   Now use the graph to solve . Note that the solution set consists of two intervals.  Write your answer with interval notation.   Next, we'll use a number line.   Translate the inequality into a sentence about distance.  Locate 3 on the number line below, and shade the points closer than 5 units from 3.  number line -10 to 10  Write your answer with interval notation.  Now use the number line to solve .  number line -10 to 10  Shade the points farther than 5 units from 3. Write your answer with interval notation.   Finally, we'll solve the inequality with algebra.  This absolute value inequality is equivalent to the compound inequality . Solve the inequality and verify that you get the same solution as before.  Now we'll solve . This absolute value inequality is equivalent to the compound inequality Solve the inequality and verify that you get the same solution as before.     More Inequalities   Solve the inequality in two ways:   Graph on the grid and use the graph to solve the inequality. Write your answer in interval notation.  grid -10 to 10 by -4 to 10  Solve algebraically. is equivalent to   Solve the inequality in two ways   Graph on the grid and use the graph to solve the inequality. Write your answer in interval notation.  grid -10 to 10 by -4 to 10  Solve algebraically. is equivalent to or     Checkpoint   How do we write \"the distance between and 5\" in mathematical notation?  How many solutions are there to the equation , if ?  Do you prefer to solve absolute value inequalities algebraically, or with a graph? Why?   "
