  "body": " Variation  Constant of Variation  Complete the statements about direct variation.   Definition: is proportional to , or varies directly with , if the ratio is .  From this fact we can write a formula for in terms of : .  The graph of a direct variation is .  The constant of variation is just the of the graph.    Tax Rate  Delbert's credit card statement lists three purchases he made while on a business trip in the Midwest. His company's accountant would like to know the sales tax rate on the purchases.    Price of Item ($)  18  28  12  Tax ($)  1.17  1.82  0.78  Tax\/Price       Compute the ratio of the tax to the price of each item. Is the tax proportional to the price? What is the tax rate?   Express the tax, , as a function of the price, , of the item.  Sketch a graph of the function.  grid [0,30]x[0,2]  What is the slope of the graph?  Look back at your work above to answer the questions.  How can you recognize a direct variation from a table of values?  How can you find the constant of variation?     Weight on the Moon  The weight of an object on the moon varies directly with its weight on earth. A person who weighs 150 pounds on earth would weigh only 24.75 pounds on the moon.   Find a formula that gives the weight of an object on the moon in terms of its weight on earth.  Complete the table.     100  150  200  400        Use technology to graph your function. Make a sketch of the graph and label the scales on the axes.  How much would a person weigh on the moon if she weighs 120 pounds on earth? Label the corresponding point on your graph.  A piece of rock weighs 50 pounds on the moon. How much will it weigh back on earth? Label the corresponding point on your graph.    Direct Variation with a Power  Complete the statements about direct variation.   The formula for direct variation with a power is .  From that formula, we see that the ratio is constant.  The graph of a direct variation always passes through .    Acceleration  At constant acceleration from rest, the distance traveled by a racecar is proportional to the square of the time elapsed. The highest recorded road-tested acceleration is 0 to 60 miles per hour in 3.07 seconds, which produces the following data.    Time (seconds)  2  2.5  3  Distance (feet)  57.32  89.563  128.97  Distance\/Time       Compute the ratios of the distance traveled to the square of the time elapsed. What is the constant of proportionality?   Express the distance traveled, , as a function of time in seconds, .  Sketch a graph of the function.  grid [0,4]x[0,150]  Look back at your work above to answer the questions.  In part (a), you computed the ratio (not the ratio ). Why?  What sort of graph do you get for the function?    Stopping Distance  The faster a car moves, the more difficult it is to stop. The graph shows the distance, , required to stop a car as a function of its velocity, , before the brakes were applied.  half of parabola on [0,50]x[0,15] through (20,2)   Find a formula for as a function of . Hints:   How do you know from the graph that (instead of ) ?  Use a point on the graph to find the value of , and then write the formula.   How fast was the car moving if it took 50 meters to stop?  What is the stopping distance for a car moving at 100 kilometers per hour?    Inverse Variation  Complete the statements about inverse variation.   The formula for inverse variation is .  An inverse variation is an example of a function.  The graph of an inverse variation has a at .  If varies inversely with , so that , what is true about the product of the variables?    Wrapping Paper  The marketing department for a paper company is testing wrapping paper rolls in various dimensions to see which shape consumers prefer. All the rolls contain the same amount of wrapping paper.    Width (feet)  2  2.5  3  Length (feet)  12  9.6  8  Length Feet      1(a) Point out that not every decreasing function represents inverse variation; we must test for .   Compute the product of the length and width for each roll of wrapping paper. What is the constant of inverse proportionality?  Express the length, of the paper as a function of the width, of the roll.  Sketch a graph of the function. Which basic graph does your answer resemble?  grid [0,8]x[0,20]     Ocean Temperature  The thermocline is a layer of ocean water where the temperature changes rapidly. The table shows the temperature of the water as a function of depth in the thermocline. What is the ocean temperature at a depth of 500 meters?    Depth (m)  200  400  1000  Temperature ( C)  20  10  4    How do you know from the table that this is an inverse variation?  Find a formula for , temperature, in terms of , depth.  What is the ocean temperature at a depth of 500 meters?    Sunshine  The intensity, , of radiation from the Sun is inversely proportional to the square of the distance, , from the Sun. Mercury is about 36 million miles from the Sun and receives radiation intensity of approximately 9000 watts per square meter.   Write a formula for as a function of .  The distance from the Sun to Earth is about three times the distance from the Sun to Mercury. What level of radiation intensity does Earth receive?  What happens to the radiation intensity if the distance from the Sun is quadrupled?    Checkpoint   How can you recognize direct or inverse variation from a graph?  What ratio should you compute to see if varies directly with ?  Is every decreasing function an inverse variation? Explain.  If you double the velocity of a car, will its stopping distance also double?   "
