  "title": "Sunshine.",
  "body": "Sunshine  The intensity, , of radiation from the Sun is inversely proportional to the square of the distance, , from the Sun. Mercury is about 36 million miles from the Sun and receives radiation intensity of approximately 9000 watts per square meter.   Write a formula for as a function of .  The distance from the Sun to Earth is about three times the distance from the Sun to Mercury. What level of radiation intensity does Earth receive?  What happens to the radiation intensity if the distance from the Sun is quadrupled?   "
