  "body": " Logarithmic Scales  Weights of Animals   The table shows the mass, or weights, of different animals. Try to plot all these values on a number line. Why is that difficult?    Animal  Shrew  Cat  Wolf  Horse  Elephant  Whale  Mass (kg)  0.004  4  80  300  5400  70,000   Instead, take the log of each animal's weight, then plot those values:    Animal  Shrew  Cat  Wolf  Horse  Elephant  Whale  Mass (kg)  0.004  4  80  300  5400  70,000  Log (Mass)         Number line:  This type of graph is called a log scale.  Consider another table of weights for some hypothetical animals.    Animal       Mass (kg)  0.6  6  60  600  6000  Log (Mass)        What do you notice about the weights of these four animals?  What do you notice about the logs of their weights?  Multiplying by a factor of 10 on a normal scale results in on a log scale.    Richter Scale  On April 30, 1986, an earthquake in Mexico City measured 7.0 on the Richter scale. On September 21 a second earthquake, measuring 8.1, hit Mexico City. How many times stronger was the September quake than the one in April?   Let denote the amplitude of the April quake, with .  Let denote the amplitude of the September quake, with  Use the formula for the Richter magnitude to calculate and in terms of (the amplitude of the smallest detectable earthquake):  Solve for :  Solve for :  Finally, compute the ratio and answer the question in the problem.    Checkpoint   How does a log scale differ from a linear scale?  What happens to the log of a number when you multiply the number by 10?  Why are log scales useful for displaying data?  In Activity 2(a), what is the first step in solving for ?   "
