  "title": "Graphing Parabolas",
  "body": " Graphing Parabolas  Graphing Practice, I  All of the grids in Activities 1 through 3 show a graph of the basic parabola, , so that you can compare it to your transformed graph.   Complete the table of values, then sketch the graph and label the coordinates of three points on the graph.   i.                 Graph of y=x^2 on [-4,4]x[-5,5]  ii.                 Graph of y=x^2 on [-4,4]x[-15,15]  Compare each graph to the basic parabola, . How is it different?     Graphing Practice, II   Complete the table of values, then sketch the graph.   i.                     Graph of y=x^2 on 10x10 grid   ii.                     Graph of y=x^2 on 10x10 grid    Find the -intercepts of each graph.  2b. If necessary, help students find the -intercepts algebraically.  Find the vertex of each graph.  Compare each graph to the basic parabola, . How is it different?     Graphing Practice, III   Complete the table of values, then sketch the graph.   i.                   Graph of y=x^2 on 10x10 grid   ii.                     Graph of y=x^2 on 10x10 grid    Find the -intercepts of each graph.  Find the vertex of each graph.  Compare each graph to the basic parabola, . How is it different?    Intercepts and Vertex    How do we find the -intercept of a parabola from its equation?  How do we find the -intercepts of a parabola from its equation?  Recall that to find the average of two numbers we add them up, and divide the result by 2. Find the average of 9 and 15.  Write an expression for the average of the numbers and .    If the -intercepts of a parabola are and , what is the -coordinate of its vertex?  If the -intercepts of a parabola are and , what is the -coordinate of its vertex?  How do we find the -coordinate of the vertex from the equation?      Stopping Distance  A car traveling at miles per hour on a wet road surface requires approximately feet to stop, where is given by the function   Make a table showing the stopping distance, , for speeds of 10, 20, ... , 100 miles per hour. (Use technology to make your table.)                           Graph the function for in terms of .   Insurance investigators at the scene of an accident find skid marks 100 feet long leading up to the point of impact. Write and solve an equation to discover how fast the car was traveling when it put on the brakes. Verify your answer on your graph.    Checkpoint   What are the -intercepts of the graph of ? What are the -intercepts of the graph of ?  What is the axis of symmetry of the graph of ? What is the axis of symmetry of the graph of ?  How is the graph of different from the basic parabola? What are the coordinates of its vertex?  Compare the graphs of and .   "
