  "body": " Graphs of Polynomial Functions  Approximating  Polynomials are easy to evaluate (especially with a computer) because they involve only the four arithmetic operations. And because they can take on such a variety of shapes, they are often used to approximate other functions.   Graph the functions on the interval . For what values of does it appear that would be a good approximation for ?   Use your calculator to fill in the table of values.                                     The difference is the error in the approximation.    Polynomial Approximation   We can reduce the error in our approximation by using a polynomial of higher degree. Replace on your graph by What is the largest error for on the interval ?  The th degree polynomial for approximating is where Graph and on the interval . (You will need to include larger -values.) What is the error in approximating by ?  Graph on the interval , with -values from to . Use the graph to estimate the largest interval on which the error is less than 0.01.  What is the smallest value of for which is less than 0.01 on the interval  What conclusions can you draw from your investigation? Write a short paragraph summarizing your results.    Shapes of Polynomials  For each description, write the equation of the polynomial of smallest degree that has the given features. Use your graphing tool to check your work.    -intercepts at and ; -intercept at  zeros at and , double zero at ; -intercept at  double zeros at and ; -intercept at  zero at , double zero at , triple zero at ; -intercept at    Checkpoint   Can you factor the polynomial in Activity 1? How do you know?  Can you factor the polynomial in Activity 2? How do you know?  How can you alter the equation for a polynomial to change its -intercept from to ?  What does the multiplicity of a zero tell you about the shape of the graph?   "
