  "title": "Equations with Fractions.",
  "body": "Equations with Fractions   If an equation contains more than one fraction, we can clear all the denominators at once by multiplying both sides by the of the fractions.  Follow the steps to solve:   Find the LCD. First factor each denominator.      Multiply each term of the equation by the LCD. If you write each denominator in its factored form, it will be easier to simplify the terms:   Simplify by reducing each term.  Solve.    "
